he effect of health beliefs and health professionals</article-title><source>Child Care Health Dev</source><year>2003</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12823336</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2214.2003.00347.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hak</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Schonbeck</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>De Melker</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Essen</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanders</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Negative attitude of highly educated parents and health care workers towards future vaccinations in the Dutch childhood vaccination program</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><year>2005</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>3103</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15837208</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.vaccine.2005.01.074</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gust</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Shui</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nowak</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Pickering</surname><given-names>LK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parent attitudes toward immunizations and healthcare providers the role of information</article-title><source>Am J Prev Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16005806</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.amepre.2005.04.010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citatio